## Smoke test 1 rerun — one-shot prompt on the default model

Canonical command per docs/smoke-testing.md. Attempt 1:
```
prime-agent -p --no-session "Reply with exactly: routing-ok"
```
Output (verbatim):
```
402 Insufficient balance (including overdraft). Please add funds to continue. Requests are authenticated by PRIME_API_KEY and billed to the personal balance unless the request includes X-Prime-Team-ID. Add funds to the selected balance. If you intended to use team billing, send X-Prime-Team-ID with the team ID and make sure that team has funds. See https://docs.primeintellect.ai/inference/troubleshooting#insufficient-funds.
exit=1
```
(real 0m1.332s)

Attempt 2 (retry 1, +5 s): identical verbatim 402, `exit=1` (real 0m0.649s).
Attempt 3 (retry 2, +20 s, final): identical verbatim 402, `exit=1`
(real 0m0.727s). Retry budget exhausted.

Documented-reroute evidence (the `providerBackupModel` tier, same command
shape as the original log's reroute check):
```
prime-agent -p --no-session --provider zai --model glm-5.3-flash "Reply with exactly: routing-ok"
```
Output (verbatim):
```
routing-ok
exit=0
```
(real 0m6.612s)

Supplementary default-route evidence from this same run (see smoke test 2):
the smoke-2 probe PARENT session — a fresh daemon-backed session with no
`--provider`/`--model` flags, i.e. the default route — ran the whole probe
on the default model with zero errors. Its session log
(`~/.prime/agent/sessions/01a12cf0-7bf9-7407-83ae-8164e48b62ef.jsonl`)
records:
```json
{"type":"model_change","id":"7b86cb0b","parentId":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:48:40.318Z","provider":"openai-codex","modelId":"gpt-6-sol"}
{"type":"thinking_level_change","id":"0bc08e66","parentId":"7b86cb0b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:48:40.318Z","thinkingLevel":"high"}
```
402 occurrences in that parent session log: **0**.

**Verdict: FAIL ON PRIMARY / PASS ON REROUTE** — the `-p` one-shot primary
route is blocked with 402 Insufficient balance (exact error above; billed
to the personal `PRIME_API_KEY` balance per the error text), identical to
the original log's finding F4 shape; the documented zai/glm-5.3-flash
reroute passed cleanly. Daemon-backed sessions on the same default route
(`openai-codex` / `gpt-6-sol` / `high`) ran fine during this same window
(see smoke test 2), so the default-route model itself is healthy — the
